      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Submit a provider text-to-image asset task. Default is async; use --wait/--poll\r\nto wait.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --prompt TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Generation prompt.\r\n          --ratio TEXT        Image ratio, e.g. 1:1, 16:9, 9:16.\r\n          --resolution-type TEXT \r\n                              Image resolution type, e.g. 2k or 4k.\r\n          --provider TEXT [pc_aigc]  \r\n                              Provider id. Default: pc_aigc (migrated PC AIGC implementation).\r\n          --provider-params-json TEXT \r\n                              Provider-specific parameters as a JSON object or @path.\r\n          --model-version TEXT \r\n                              Provider model version.\r\n          --download-dir TEXT Directory for generated assets when waiting or querying.\r\n          --download-format TEXT:{png,jpeg} \r\n                              Convert downloaded image assets to png or jpeg. Omit to preserve\r\n                              provider format.\r\n          --poll <seconds>    Maximum whole seconds to wait; accepts 60 or 60s. Default 0,\r\n                              submit only.\r\n          --wait              Wait up to the default timeout for generation result.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media aigc text2image --prompt \"a cat portrait\" --ratio 1:1 --resolution-type 2k\r\n",
